<h2>A Clearer View of Our Services</h2>
<p>Our services are now organized into four areas:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/architectural-scale-models">Architectural and real estate models</a></li>
<li><a href="/scale-model-services/product">Product prototypes and mockups</a></li>
<li><a href="/scale-model-services/film">Film and commercial miniatures</a></li>
<li><a href="/scale-model-services/art">Art maquettes and prototypes</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Each service page explains the different model types, what they are used to evaluate, and which teams typically use them.</p>

<h2>More Transparency Throughout the Process</h2>
<p>The new <a href="/model-making-process">model-making process</a> section explains how projects move from initial definition and digital preparation through fabrication, quality control, packaging, and delivery.</p>
<p>We have also expanded our <a href="/blog">Journal</a> with practical guidance on model scale, cost, production timelines, project briefs, materials, transportation, and the transition from digital design to physical fabrication.</p>

<h2>Carve Studio Portal in Partner Testing</h2>
<p>The Carve Studio Portal is currently being tested with selected partners ahead of its expected broader launch in January 2027.</p>
<p>The Portal is being developed to bring project milestones, files, feedback, approvals, messages, quality-control updates, invoices, and delivery information into one organized workspace.</p>
<p>Read more about the <a href="/blog/carve-studio-portal-partner-testing">Carve Studio Portal partner-testing program</a>.</p>

<h2>Built to Continue Evolving</h2>
<p>The website will continue to grow with additional project work, technical guidance, and studio updates.</p>
<p>The new website reflects the same principle that guides our model-making work: provide the right information, reduce uncertainty, and help teams move forward with confidence.</p>
